 CROSS-SECTION EVALUATION PROCEDURE                               2722 1451  190
                                                                  2722 1451  191
 Adopted procedure is based on careful theoretical                2722 1451  192
 analysis utilizing available experimental data and               2722 1451  193
 nuclear reaction model calculations.                             2722 1451  194
                                                                  2722 1451  195
 Available experimental data were interpreted  using              2722 1451  196
 nuclear reaction model code EMPIRE-3 by M. Herman                2722 1451  197
 et al [EMP]. This code integrates into a single                  2722 1451  198
 system a number of important modules and features:               2722 1451  199
                                                                  2722 1451  200
 - Spherical and deformed Optical Model including                 2722 1451  201
   coupled-channels (ECIS06 by J. Raynal)                         2722 1451  202
 - Hauser-Feshbach statistical model including                    2722 1451  203
   HRTW width fluctuation correction                              2722 1451  204
 - Quantum-mechanical MSD TUL model (codes ORION &                2722 1451  205
   TRISTAN by H. Lenske), and MSC NVWY model                      2722 1451  206
 - Exciton model with angular momentum coupling                   2722 1451  207
   (code DEGAS by E. Betak and P. Oblozinsky) that                2722 1451  208
   represents a good approximation to the DSD model               2722 1451  209
 - Exciton model with Iwamoto-Harada cluster                      2722 1451  210
   emission and Kalbach systematic angular distr.                 2722 1451  211
   (code PCROSS by R.Capote et al)                                2722 1451  212
 - Complete gamma-ray cascade after emission of                   2722 1451  213
   each particle, including realistic treatment of                2722 1451  214
   discrete transitions                                           2722 1451  215
 - Access to OM segment of the RIPL library [RIPL]                2722 1451  216
 - Built-in input parameter files, such as masses,                2722 1451  217
   level density, discrete levels, fission barriers               2722 1451  218
   and gamma strength functions based on the RIPL                 2722 1451  219
   library [RIPL]                                                 2722 1451  220
 - Automatic retrieval of experimental data from the              2722 1451  221
   EXFOR/CSISRS library                                           2722 1451  222
 - ENDF-6 formatting (code EMPEND by A. Trkov)                    2722 1451  223
   coupled to graphical presentation capabilities                 2722 1451  224
   (code ZVView by V. Zerkin) through the chain of                2722 1451  225
   PrePro codes by R. Cullen                                      2722 1451  226
 - Checking codes (CHECKR, FIZCON, PSYCHE)                        2722 1451  227
 - Support for NJOY                                               2722 1451  228
                                                                  2722 1451  229
